# Catalogue content

Author definitions as TypeScript data in:

- Tactics → `cards.ts`
- Creatures → `creatures.ts`
- Faces → `faces.ts`

Rules:

- `rulesText` / print fields are English authority for the UI.
- Structured regions (`effect`, `equipment`, `overload`, `ritual`, attack `effect`, face `onRoll`) only when every clause is modelled.
- Ids: `card-<kebab>`, `creature-<kebab>`, `face-natural|synthetic|untyped-<kebab>`, `attack-<creature>-<kebab>`.
- `equipment` / `overload` are main `CardType` values and must match their regions (and vice versa).
- Rituals use main `type: "ritual"` with ritual subtypes (`instant` / `continuous` / `reaction`) and must have a `ritual` region.
- Update `docs/specs/002|003|004-*.md` and `docs/DEFERRED_CATALOGUE.md` when print coverage changes.
- Dual-timing faces use `On roll:` / `On absorb:` print; see `.cursor/skills/standardize-card-effects/`.
- Synthetic faces are **named specials only**. Never author blank generics
  (`face-synthetic-martial`, `face-synthetic-corruption`, Forged Martial, …).
- Follow `.cursor/skills/author-content/SKILL.md` for full workflows and templates.
